From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port Bot <port@local>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:40:00 +0200
Subject: fix: default missing rule alerts to empty array (notification bell)

vmalert (VictoriaMetrics) omits `alerts` entirely on rules with no active
alerts, unlike Prometheus which always includes `alerts: []`. Console
core's own copy of getAlertsAndRules() (frontend/public/components/monitoring/utils.ts)
then calls rule.alerts.forEach()/rule.alerts.map() on undefined, breaking
the notification bell/drawer with "TypeError: can't access property
forEach, e.alerts is undefined". This is the same bug already patched in
plugins/monitoring's own copy of this function
(0001-default-missing-rule-alerts-to-empty-array.patch) - console core
has an independent copy consumed by useNotificationPoller /
useNamespacedNotificationAlertsPoller, which this repo's monitoring
plugin build never touches. See plugins/monitoring/VICTORIA-METRICS-TODO.md
item 1.

---
 frontend/public/components/monitoring/utils.ts | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/frontend/public/components/monitoring/utils.ts b/frontend/public/components/monitoring/utils.ts
index 5acfdcdd..2f18c1da 100644
--- a/frontend/public/components/monitoring/utils.ts
+++ b/frontend/public/components/monitoring/utils.ts
@@ -53,7 +53,9 @@ export const getAlertsAndRules = (
         r.query,
         ..._.map(r.labels, (k, v) => `${k}=${v}`),
       ].join(',');
-      return { ...r, id: String(murmur3(key, 'monitoring-salt')) };
+      // vmalert (VictoriaMetrics) omits `alerts` entirely for rules with no
+      // active alerts, unlike Prometheus which always includes `alerts: []`.
+      return { ...r, alerts: r.alerts ?? [], id: String(murmur3(key, 'monitoring-salt')) };
     };

     return _.filter(g.rules, { type: 'alerting' }).map(addID);
